Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: Seek medical attention right away if you have symptoms of serotonin syndrome, such as: agitation, hallucinations, fever, sweating, shivering, fast heart rate, muscle stiffness, twitching, loss of coordination, nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea.
Common venlafaxine side effects may include:
- headache, dizziness, drowsiness, tiredness;
- ringing in your ears, feeling anxious, nervous, or jittery;
- sleep problems, unusual dreams;
- tremors;
- fast heartbeats;
- blurred vision;
- nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation;
- changes in weight or appetite;
- dry mouth, yawning;
- increased sweating; or
- sexual problems.
This is not a complete list of side effects and others may occur. Call your doctor for medical advice about side effects. You may report side effects to FDA at 1-800-FDA-1088.
Triplet: ["serotonin syndrome", "has symptom", "nausea"]

The relation 'has symptom' in the triplet is defined as 'The condition or medical state specified by the object entity includes the symptom specified by the subject entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'mimics symptoms of': The subject condition or drug may present symptoms that resemble those of the medical condition specified by the object entity.
B. 'can occur with': The subject drug can be present in individuals who also have the condition specified by the object entity.
C. 'treats': The subject drug is used to treat or manage the disease or medical condition specified by the object entity.
D. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
E. 'can cause damage to': The condition specified by the object entity may result in physical or functional damage to the organ or tissue specified by the subject entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
